From: Super Protocol VM Tools <devnull@superprotocol.com>
Subject: qemu: provide TDX VM type UAPI constants for older build headers

Ubuntu 24.04 build environments can provide linux-libc-dev headers that do
not define the KVM VM-types capability or the x86 TDX VM type.  libvirt then
compiles virQEMUCapsKVMSupportsVMTypeTDX() as an unconditional false result,
even when the runtime kernel advertises TDX through KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES.

Keep the runtime capability check enabled when building on x86_64.  Kernels
that do not implement KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES safely return zero for the unknown
KVM_CHECK_EXTENSION capability.

--- a/src/qemu/qemu_capabilities.c
+++ b/src/qemu/qemu_capabilities.c
@@ -56,6 +56,20 @@
 #ifdef WITH_LINUX_KVM_H
 # include <linux/kvm.h>
 # include <sys/ioctl.h>
+/*
+ * KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES and KVM_X86_TDX_VM are runtime ABI values.  Some older
+ * distro linux-libc-dev packages omit them even though the libvirt package is
+ * intended to run with a newer, TDX-capable kernel.  Without both macros the
+ * TDX probe below is compiled into the "KVM not compiled" fallback.
+ */
+# if defined(__x86_64__)
+#  ifndef KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES
+#   define KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES 235
+#  endif
+#  ifndef KVM_X86_TDX_VM
+#   define KVM_X86_TDX_VM 5
+#  endif
+# endif
 #endif
 
 #define VIR_FROM_THIS VIR_FROM_QEMU
